hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16721","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Ashath, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from a man of his people, he said: He used to say during the caliphate of Umar ibn al-Khattab: Uthman will not die until he is made caliph; we said: From where do you know that; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I saw tonight in a dream as if three of my companions were weighed; Abu Bakr was weighed and outweighed, then Umar was weighed and outweighed, then Uthman was weighed and our companion fell short, though he is righteous."
